; Tabitha, the full theme from sketch E "Stupid Weak People": G minor, 120 bpm, a 2-bar intro and a 32-bar loop (about 64 s). A trumpet speaks a sneering hook in the rhythm of her words over chopped cold strings, a bass on the beats, a snare march and timpani (A); the hook goes a fourth up through C minor and A flat and falls to D7 (B); a horn sings over held strings and a lighter march in B flat major (C); the hook returns with the horn doubling it an octave down and a fuller kit (A2).
; Trumpet A.56, strings A.48, bass A.34, kit A.120, timpani A.47, horn A.111. Original notes, AW2 voices, no rom lines.
song tabitha
tempo 120
meter 4/4
reverb 173
priority 0

inst trump = A.56 shift=-12
inst str = A.48 shift=0
inst bass = A.34 shift=24
inst kit = A.120
inst timp = A.47 shift=24
inst horn = A.111 shift=-12
hit kick=36 rim=37 clap=39 snare=40 hat=44 ohat=46 tom1=45 tom2=48 tom3=50 crash=49

